+# T-207 handoff — Activate the M2 acceptance suite (A-201..A-209)
+
+BLOCKED: A-208 (holdout variant) unmet — `POST /admin/lights/{id}` silently
+ignores a posted `kind` change, so the frozen holdout draft
+`TestHoldoutA208EditKindAndSoftDelete` (kind-only edit park→building must
+persist while label/asset/photo keep values) fails at
+`admin_lights_holdout_test.go:376` ("detail page after edit lacks
+\"Building\""; the detail still renders `Kind: park`). The feature matches its
+own governing packet — T-205 freezes "edit (label, asset_no; unspecified
+fields keep values)" and `internal/web/admin.go:423-477` (`adminEdit` +
+`parseLightEdit`) implements exactly that, with no Kind field in the detail
+form — while the frozen holdout oracle (T-200) asserts kind editability under
+the drafts README's generic "multipart `csrf_token` + changed fields" edit
+row. The visible suite never edits kind (Go draft edits label only; e2e edits
+label only), so no visible spec conflicts. Per the activation rules I did NOT
+edit the test; it is left red as the routed dispute. Planner options: (a) cut
+a small fix task in `internal/web` + the detail template to accept/apply a
+`kind` edit (parse + validate `park|building` + store write + form select), or
+(b) re-freeze the holdout A-208 variant to edit a different field. Every other
+M2 spec — visible and holdout — is green.
+
